The accompanying openal-soft-1.21.1.patch fixes one optional member access for
current compilers and confines the private component to built-in defaults and
its upstream HRTF data, without reading user OpenAL settings or changing the
process environment. Hardware backends and utilities are disabled at build
time. The shared library remains separately replaceable and is not statically
linked into linux-wallpaperengine. Distributors must retain the license,
notices, patch and corresponding source availability required by the license.
